== notes ==

* hx1k FITS: 495/1280 logic cells (38%), so the icestick build is real,
  not just the hx8k. Both boards PASS icetime at 12 MHz with ~3x margin.
* ICESTORM_RAM = 0: yosys mapped sine_lut's 2048-bit quarter table to
  LUTs/FFs ('using FF mapping for memory theremin_top.u_lut'), not BRAM.
  The ROM read feeds the sign-negation mux BEFORE the output register,
  so memory_dff cannot merge the register into a synchronous read port
  and iCE40 BRAM (which needs one) is off the table. Costs ~10% of hx1k
  (~130 LCs; lesson07 measured 132 SB_LUT4 standalone);
  acceptable here, and a good lesson14 discussion point (lesson07 covers
  the stat line to check).
* Critical path (icetime, both boards): inside u_map (pitch_map), the
  map->clamp->smooth arithmetic feeding fcw_r — ~28 ns, comfortably
  under the 83.3 ns budget at 12 MHz.
